REMEDIATE STORY #394 (a journal-lock timeout while a seat is working ends the engine and throws the seat's attempt away) on branch story-394-contention-in-flight, already checked out in this worktree (HEAD 39b7e5f0, one signed commit on main 5921f900).

Commit 39b7e5f0 defers a working seat's contended checkpoints in an ordered hold, retries them without waiting, and settles a terminal event through the lawful end. The run implement-story-394-a-journal-lo-c4719329 parked on REVIEW-REFORGE-EXHAUSTED-MEDIUM (no security residual), and the operator ruled. Add ONE commit on top that answers the three findings below. Do not redo the story, and do not reopen what the operator ruled.

OPERATOR RULING (2026-09-28), binding on this run and its reviewers:
- The bounded settlement is ACCEPTED as designed: three settling patiences for held checkpoints, three for a terminal event, three more in the lawful end, and the 16 MiB hold (HELD_BYTES) plus one row. Past the bound, the attempt is found open and the next resume settles it as restarted. Acceptance 2's literal "never an unsettled attempt" is unsatisfiable while nothing is writable, and it is ruled out of scope.
- Findings from the parked review that are CLOSED by ruling. Do not implement them, and do not raise them again as returns:
  - 1: the bound;
  - 2: the spill file and attempt-wide bound, which move to #433;
  - 3: the retry timer;
  - 4: drain batching and the lock ticket;
  - 5: uncounted drops behind a fence refusal;
  - 7: HeldOutcome carries a Value;
  - 11: offer() serializes to measure.
  Items 3, 4, 5 and 11 are filed as #464.
- Finding 6 (no live Claude or Codex probe that no seat outlives a dead engine) is a HOST step the controller runs at landing. List it as pending in your notes.

FIRST, fetch origin and check origin/main. If it has moved past 5921f900, rebase onto it. If quality/suppressions.txt or a quality/public-api snapshot conflicts, take main's side and list it in notes for the controller to regenerate. Grep every conflicted file for markers before you continue.

1. Finding 10, the exact-coverage gate. drive()'s new arm, `if let Some(end) = self.lawful_end_under_contention(error)? { return Ok(end); }` (crates/brokkr-runtime/src/engine.rs, around lines 516-517), is never taken through drive(). The chief's llvm-cov over the contention tests shows DA:517,0 and BRDA:516,0,0,0, while the None branch is taken. Every lawful park in the suite calls lawful_end_under_contention directly. Add one test in engine/contention_tests.rs that goes through drive() into a peer's lock at a parkable cursor, where the lock lets go within the lawful end's window. It must assert the exact journaled end, and show the arm is taken. Prove it with `cargo +nightly llvm-cov -p brokkr-runtime --lib --branch --lcov` (the pinned nightly the chief used was nightly-2026-09-05) filtered to that test, and quote the DA and BRDA lines for engine.rs:516-517 in your notes. Give the test a compiling removal control that fails it: return the error instead of the end.
2. Finding 9, docs. docs/guides/quickstart.md (around lines 666-673) says a terminal event gets six patiences in all. With checkpoints held when the seat stops, settle spends three more first (engine/checkpoints.rs, around line 195), so the wait can reach nine. Each engine-side marker a panel member or a sequence step journals (engine.rs, around lines 2141 and 2569) gets three of its own. State the true bound in one short paragraph, and keep the pointer to #430.
3. Finding 8, the house semantic-change rule. The commit changed journal-visible semantics, and no decision says so. Write a short PROPOSED addendum (status: proposed, for the operator to accept; never mark it accepted) to decision 0029 (the fenced append), unless you find a decision that owns attempt settlement more directly, in which case say which and why in notes. It must name:
   - the three settling patiences for held checkpoints, and the three plus three for a terminal event;
   - the 16 MiB hold;
   - that lost or stranded evidence settles its site indeterminate;
   - that a stopped attempt is settled at EffectInFlight;
   - that past the bound the attempt is left open for resume to settle as restarted;
   - and the operator's 2026-09-28 ruling that accepted the bound.
   Add its index row if docs/decisions/README.md lists addenda. Note that #403's branch adds a proposed addendum to decision 0006, so do not touch 0006.

Gates, all clean, from the worktree root:
- cargo fmt --all -- --check
- cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings
- cargo test -p brokkr-runtime -p brokkr-store, and cargo test -p brokkr-cli --lib --test suppressions
- typos --hidden
- quality/ratchet.sh files and clones
- git diff --check origin/main..HEAD

Moved or grown functions are judged by the complexity ratchet (a new one at the ceiling of 15; an existing one at max(its baseline, 15)), so keep each function's CC within that. Do not run scripts/coverage-exact.sh; the controller runs it with the crap and api ratchets. Run everything in the foreground and never end your turn with a background job or a scheduled wake-up pending.

Commit: one commit, signed off (git commit -s), message "<area>: <what changed> (#394)", ending with "Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>". Never push. Every claim in your notes points to a command you ran and what it printed.
